#. ja: 汎用規格トームストーン v2.0
#. de: universell[a] antik[a] Stein[p] 2.0
#. fr: modèle générique de mémoquartz v2.0
#. column 2: universal tomestones 2.0
#. column 8: After a failed first attempt at creating a universal tomestone, researchers of eld upheld their focus on versatility while making allowances for utility and practicality. Featuring marked improvements to transfer capacity and data storage limits, this iteration allegedly proved somewhat popular.
#. column 9: Universal Tomestone 2.0
msgctxt "Item:46728:0:0"
msgid "universal tomestone 2.0"
msgstr "универсальный томстоун 2.0"

#. de: universell[a] antik[a] Steine[p] 2.0
#. fr: modèles génériques de mémoquartz v2.0
#. column 0: universal tomestone 2.0
#. column 8: After a failed first attempt at creating a universal tomestone, researchers of eld upheld their focus on versatility while making allowances for utility and practicality. Featuring marked improvements to transfer capacity and data storage limits, this iteration allegedly proved somewhat popular.
#. column 9: Universal Tomestone 2.0
msgctxt "Item:46728:0:2"
msgid "universal tomestones 2.0"
msgstr "универсальные томстоуны 2.0"

#. ja: 古代の記憶が記された過ぎし文明の遺物。汎用性を保ちつつ改善が施され、それなりに普及した
#. de: Ein seltener und wunderschöner Stein einer antiken Kultur, der Unmengen von uraltem Wissen enthält. Basierend auf dem originalen Stein wurde diese Version weiter verbessert, wodurch sie wohl eine gute Menge an Beliebtheit erlangte.
#. fr: Cette pierre, vestige d'une civilisation disparue, renferme des con<shy>nais<shy>san<shy>ces ancestrales. Bien qu'elle conserve un aspect générique, elle a été suf<shy>fi<shy>sam<shy>ment améliorée pour lui permettre d'être plus largement adoptée.
#. column 0: universal tomestone 2.0
#. column 2: universal tomestones 2.0
#. column 9: Universal Tomestone 2.0
msgctxt "Item:46728:0:8"
msgid "After a failed first attempt at creating a universal tomestone, researchers of eld upheld their focus on versatility while making allowances for utility and practicality. Featuring marked improvements to transfer capacity and data storage limits, this iteration allegedly proved somewhat popular."
msgstr "После неудачной первой попытки создать универсальный томстоун учёные древности не отказались от идеи универсальности, но учли удобство и практичность. Эту версию значительно улучшили: увеличили скорость передачи данных и объём хранилища. Говорят, она пользовалась некоторой популярностью."

#. ja: 汎用規格トームストーン v2.0
